   "subject": "Re: editing legend items",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi:<p>First of all, thank you for the reproducible example.<p>Scales are one of the more difficult features of ggplot2 to master,<br>and a few things are going on here that you need to learn about:<p>  (i) You can define labels in a separate vector or as labels in a<br>factor() statement; since you want expressions, the former is<br>advisable in this case.<br>  (ii) When you map multiple aesthetics to the same variable and want<br>to use a single legend, you need to modify all legends with a suitable<br>scale_*() function, one for each aesthetic defined.<br>  (iii) You can modify a title either by picking a suitable variable<br>name for the factor of interest (which will be the default legend<br>title) or you can change it manually inside a scale_*() function.<p>Here&#39;s a way to get what I think you want with the legend:<p># Create a factor variable for treatment rather than a character<br>variable so that you can control the ordering of the levels:<br>melt.M2$treat &lt;- factor(melt.M2$Treat, levels = c(&#39;2M0001&#39;, &#39;2M0010&#39;, &#39;2M0100&#39;))<p># Create a list of expressions that can be passed into the scale<br>functions as the labels = argument:<br>labls &lt;- list(expression(paste(&#39;1&#39;, mu, &#39;M&#39;, sep = &quot;&quot;)),<br>               expression(paste(&#39;10&#39;, mu, &#39;M&#39;, sep = &quot;&quot;)),<br>               expression(paste(&#39;100&#39;, mu, &#39;M&#39;, sep = &quot;&quot;)))<p>ggplot(data = melt.M2, aes(x = Time, y = value, color = treat, fill = treat)) +<br>    stat_summary(fun.data=&quot;mean_cl_normal&quot;, geom=&quot;smooth&quot;, size=1, alpha=0.1) +<br>    scale_x_continuous(limits = c(0, 48)) +<br>    scale_color_manual(&#39;My title&#39;, breaks = levels(melt.M2$treat),<br>                                   values = c(&#39;blue&#39;, &#39;green&#39;, &#39;orange&#39;),<br>                                   labels = labls) +<br>    scale_fill_manual(&#39;My title&#39;, breaks = levels(melt.M2$treat),<br>                                  values = c(&#39;blue&#39;, &#39;green&#39;, &#39;orange&#39;),<br>                                  labels = labls)<p>Notice that both scale_color_manual() and scale_fill_manual() needed<br>to be used in order for the two legends to merge. More specifically,<br>the two legends need the same title, the same breaks, the same values<br>and the same labels for the merger to take place.<p>You don&#39;t need guide_legend() here unless you want to change aspects<br>of the legend that are under its control, which are described on its<br>help page.<p>HTH,<br>Dennis<p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<p><p><p><p><p><p><p><p><p><p><p>On Thu, Mar 29, 2012 at 3:37 AM, Falko &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">r.proje...@googlemail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt; Hi there ggplot-Folks!<br>&gt;<br>&gt; I&#39;m quite new to &quot;R&quot; and &quot;ggplot&quot; and I have an issue regarding the legend<br>&gt; editing. Here is my code. I know, it might not be that elegant it could be,<br>&gt; but it works fine for me (but if you have any further suggestions - sharing<br>&gt; them would be highly appreciated)<br>&gt;<br>&gt; First of all I load my raw-data, which I gained from an RTCA-experiment:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; library(gplots)<br>&gt; mcpd2&lt;-read.xls(&quot;<a href=\"http://dl.dropbox.com/u/19497400/Data/20110929_raw_Caco2_copy.xls\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dl.dropbox.com/u/19497400/Data/20110929_raw_Caco2_copy.xls&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792376409429000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1K9KeMi-TxWrpMsKAfrRge\">http://dl.dropbox.com/u/19497400/Data/20110929_raw_Caco2_copy.xls</a>&quot;,sheet=1)<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Now that I have my data, I&#39;ve got to rename the columns:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; colnames(mcpd2)&lt;-c(&quot;Time&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;Hours&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M1000_A&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M1000_B&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M1000_C&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0500_A&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0500_B&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0500_C&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0250_A&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0250_B&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0250_C&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0100_A&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0100_B&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0100_C&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0050_A&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0050_B&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0050_C&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0025_A&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0025_B&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0025_C&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0010_A&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0010_B&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0010_C&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0001_A&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0001_B&quot;,<br>&gt;                    &quot;2M0001_C&quot;<br>&gt;                    )<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Now, I have to normalize to a certain timepoint by typing:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; mcpd2.s&lt;-<br>&gt; as.data.frame(<br>&gt; sweep(<br>&gt; data.matrix(mcpd2),<br>&gt; 2,<br>&gt; data.matrix(mcpd2)[93,]<br>&gt; )<br>&gt; )<br>&gt;<br>&gt; That done, I pick the concentrations I&#39;d like to plot:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; pick&lt;-c(&quot;Time&quot;,&quot;01&quot;)<br>&gt; picked&lt;-unique(<br>&gt; grep(<br>&gt; paste(<br>&gt; pick,<br>&gt; collapse=&quot;|&quot;<br>&gt; ),<br>&gt; colnames(mcpd2.s),<br>&gt; value=TRUE<br>&gt; )<br>&gt; )<br>&gt; toPlot&lt;-mcpd2.s[picked]<br>&gt;<br>&gt; After that I melt the data obtained and make a colsplit with the<br>&gt; reshape2-package:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; melt.M2.a&lt;-melt(toPlot,id.var=&quot;Time&quot;)<br>&gt; melt.M2&lt;-<br>&gt; cbind(<br>&gt; melt.M2.a,<br>&gt; reshape2::colsplit(melt.M2.a$variable,&quot;_&quot;,c(&quot;Treat&quot;,&quot;Replicate&quot;))<br>&gt; )<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Now the plot can be created:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; library(ggplot)<br>&gt; plot.M2&lt;-ggplot(data=melt.M2,aes(x=Time,y=value,group=Treat,color=Treat,fill=Treat))<br>&gt; plot.M2+<br>&gt;   stat_summary(fun.data=&quot;mean_cl_normal&quot;,geom=&quot;smooth&quot;,size=1,alpha=0.1)+<br>&gt;   scale_x_continuous(limits=c(0,48))<br>&gt;<br>&gt; And here is where I got stuck. How can I edit the legend, the legend title<br>&gt; itself and also what is written within the legend. Is there a way to change<br>&gt; &quot;2M0001&quot; into &quot;1µM&quot;. By adding the code line:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; +guides(fill=guide_legend(title=&quot;title&quot;))<br>&gt;<br>&gt; it just gives me a second legend with the desired title but doesn&#39;t replace<br>&gt; the actual one. Also, the colors don&#39;t match with the graph and the legend<br>&gt; items are not renamed. Am I missing something?<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Any hint is highly appreciated.<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Regards,<br>&gt; Falko<br>&gt;<br></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p>"
